n.\n\n**One carry-forward note, not blocking.** `V2AdmittedModels` refuses a v2 ordered ceiling for a runtime the frozen snapshot never captured; the source's own adapter (`admission_registry.go:69-90`) instead falls back to the live registry. I verified this against the source binary, not by reading it — a scratch config with a `gemini` ceiling makes the source admit all seven live gemini rows while discarding the bound entirely. It doesn't touch AC4 (the source config carries only codex and claude ceilings, both captured), the port states the choice explicitly, and its refusal is the safer behaviour. Recorded in the verdict so the config/preflight port story meets it as an argued divergence rather than a surprise.\n\nVerdict artifact: `TASK-260822-3cknas_review-verdict.md`. Review evidence under `.temp/TASK-260822-3cknas-review/`.","ttft_ms":3404,"ttft_stream_ms":2658,"time_to_request_ms":21,"type":"result","duration_ms":663504,"uuid":"1fe7894f-e265-47ef-a08e-15a7431610b0"}
